  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Hazari. 52 cards, 4 players. Phase 1: Partition 13 cards into 3-3-3-4 sets. Phase 2: Sequential comparison of sets using Brag rankings (Troy > Color Run > Run > Color > Pair > High). Scoring: A, K, Q, J, 10 = 10 pts each. Target: 1000.',
    Player: "Welcome to Hazari! You have 13 cards. Divide them into four sets: three sets of 3 cards and one set of four. Call 'Up' when you're ready to compare. High cards (A, K, Q, J, 10) are your point gold! First to 1000 wins.",
    objective: 'Be the first player to reach a cumulative score of 1000 points by winning card comparisons.',
    gameplay: "1. PARTITIONING: Each player arranges their 13 cards into four sets. Three sets contain 3 cards each, and the fourth (final) set contains 4 cards. Players must arrange them so they are played from strongest to weakest (though this is a strategy, not a restriction).\n2. CALLING: When all players have partitioned their cards, they call 'Up' or 'Ready'.\n3. COMPARISONS: There are four rounds of comparison. In each, players reveal one set. The winner of a comparison takes all cards from that round. The winner of Comparison 1 leads Comparison 2, and so on.\n4. POINT SCORING: High cards (A, K, Q, J, 10) are worth 10 points each. Other cards (2-9) are worth 0 points.",
    keyRules: [
      'Ranking of 3rd-card sets (highest to lowest): 1. Troy (Three of a Kind), 2. Color Run (Straight Flush), 3. Run (Straight), 4. Color (Flush), 5. Pair, 6. High Card.',
      'Points: A=10, K=10, Q=10, J=10, 10=10.',
      'Total points in the deck are 200.',
      'If sets are equal in rank, the highest card within the set determines the winner.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
